	(text "The bank is the soft start for everything: BMS sees no inrush. Reset closes it, loop open drops it. No software in the path.\nRs 0.5 mOhm: limit 97-123 A (VCL 48.5-61.5 mV), breaker 160-260 A (VCB 80-130 mV). Above peak draw and JK DOC 80 A. 1.8 W at 60 A.\nStart: Cdv 100 nF, gate 10-22 uA, 100-220 V/s, 0.25-0.55 s to full. Bus ceiling 9.4 mF at 2.06 A hot DC SOA line (112 W, 45 K Tj rise). Drive caps unmeasured.\nPower limit 544 W, RPWR = 125k x Rs x P, 5 mV floor per SNVS452G sec 9.2.1.2.3. Timer 22 nF: 1.0 ms typ, 1.8 ms max.\nFault check: 675 W (+24 %) is 12.4 A at 54.6 V against about 15 A at 1.8 ms, 70 C, one FET, scaled from the 10 ms curve as sqrt(t). Read the real curve at layout.\nFETs: 0.85 mOhm for the pair, 5.2 W hot at 60 A, 1.3 W at 30 A. UVLO low sinks the gate at 2 mA: about 170 us off.\nBody diodes pass regen back to the pack with the bank open. OVLO tied low: opening on overvoltage would strand regen on the bus.\nLM5069-1 latches on a fault. Clear: E-stop cycle, then reset. PGD (open drain) holds the brick off until the bus is up, per TI's keep-the-load-off note.\nSMDJ58A: catches the battery lead's inductive kick when the bank opens. Clears 54.6 V, FETs and U1 are 100 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 300 92 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c1c04571-fb02-597e-b720-a21eb5faf37d")
	)
	(text "2. Control rail and E-stop latch (no logic IC)"
