	(text "Seal-in latch, ngspice checked at hFE 80: stays off at power-up even with reset held, reset closes it, a 50 us contact bounce rides through,\nloop open drops it in about 100 us, re-closing the loop does nothing, a reset held through a loop cycle does nothing, a new press works 5 ms after release.\nRUN 7 V (UVLO 3.5 V): needs 5.7-6.1 V rising, so it holds. Loses VCTL, RUN drops, UVLO drops: bank opens.\nLoop 6 mA, wetting for a control-rated NC contact. No 12 V on the connector without a series R, pin 1 next to GND: a short there opens the loop.\nBrake resistor NC thermostat: wire it in series in the loop harness, no board parts. E-stop model still to confirm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 284.48 240 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "678ac5fc-6678-53c0-8ace-a6b2d71ab36f")
	)
	(text "3. Braking clamp: 56.8 V on, 55.8 V off, 57.5 V worst case, into the HS25"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 262 0)
		(effects
