	(text "On the bus, so the brick drops with the E-stop and the Pi goes with it. PGD on R.C keeps it off during the ramp: it starts at 9 V and would load the FETs mid-ramp.\n-Vout is tied to GND here: the robot has one ground, P-. RS+ and RS- tied at the pins, Trim open. Input caps at the pins; the EMC filter is left out.\n150 W at 12 V, 89 %: 18 W at full load, about 6 W at 50 W. Natural-air derating starts near 30 C. 12.7 mm tall: keep clear of the fan gap.\nINA228 addresses: L arm 0x40, R arm 0x41, waist 0x42, aux 0x43, L leg 0x44, R leg 0x45, 12 V 0x46. Powered by the Pi's 3.3 V; Pi pull-ups on I2C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 404 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b368fe73-c0f3-51bc-ba4b-447efd16e041")
	)
	(text "6. Limb outputs: terminal pair, 1 mOhm shunt, INA228. Fuses inline in the pigtails."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 645 22 0)
		(effects
